  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "A Muslim or Amazigh first name and a fixed family name passed down from the father, set by the civil registry in the late 1800s. Family names often start with Ben or Bel (son of), Bou (father of, or owner of), or in Kabylie with Aït (the people of). Arabic names are written in the French way: Djamel, Abdelkader, Khadidja. Kabyle families also give Amazigh names like Massinissa, Yuba, Thiziri and Dihia. On forms the family name comes first.",
